    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac{1}{2}$, because coin tosses are independent.",
      "worked": "The coin is fair, so $P(\\text{heads})=\\frac{1}{2}$. Coin tosses are independent, so the first nine results do not change the probability on the tenth toss.",
